From: Julian Decker <git@deckerjulian.com>
Subject: PCI: rockchip-host: give the PHYs back exactly once on failure

rockchip_pcie_host_init_port() releases the PHYs itself when the port
set-up or gen1 training fails, and rockchip_pcie_probe() released them
again through its error path. phy_exit() on a PHY that is already down
leaves init_count below zero, and phy_init() only calls the driver when the
count is exactly zero, so the next load runs with uninitialised PHYs and
cannot train until a reset.

The rule is now that whoever took the PHYs gives them back on failure, and
the caller does nothing:

rockchip_pcie_host_init_port() also does so when the LTSSM does not reach
L0. It used to return there with the PHYs held, leaving them to the probe,
whose rockchip_pcie_deinit_phys() skips the power off at that point because
lanes_map is not set yet.

rockchip_pcie_really_probe() releases them for its failures after a good
rockchip_pcie_host_init_port(). This keeps them balanced for the sysfs
trigger of deferred probing as well, which has no error path of its own.

rockchip_pcie_probe() no longer releases them after a failed
rockchip_pcie_really_probe(). Its remaining use of that label is the DMA
set-up failing after a good probe. There it releases them only if it has
them: with deferred probing they have not been taken at that point.

---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
@@ -383,7 +383,7 @@
 				 timeouts * USEC_PER_MSEC);
 	if (err) {
 		dev_err(dev, "LTSSM is not L0!\n");
-		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+		goto err_power_off_phy;
 	}
 
 	if (rockchip->link_gen == 2) {
@@ -1072,20 +1072,28 @@
 
 	err = rockchip_pcie_setup_irq(rockchip);
 	if (err)
-		return err;
+		goto err_deinit_phys;
 
 	rockchip_pcie_enable_interrupts(rockchip);
 
 	err = rockchip_pcie_cfg_atu(rockchip);
 	if (err)
-		return err;
+		goto err_deinit_phys;
 
 	rockchip->bridge->sysdata = rockchip;
 	rockchip->bridge->ops = &rockchip_pcie_ops;
 
 	device_init_wakeup(rockchip->dev, true);
 
-	return pci_host_probe(rockchip->bridge);
+	err = pci_host_probe(rockchip->bridge);
+	if (err)
+		goto err_deinit_phys;
+
+	return 0;
+
+err_deinit_phys:
+	rockchip_pcie_deinit_phys(rockchip);
+	return err;
 }
 
 static ssize_t pcie_deferred_store(struct device *dev,
@@ -1198,7 +1206,7 @@
 		err = rockchip_pcie_really_probe(rockchip);
 		if (err) {
 			dev_err(&pdev->dev, "deferred probe failed\n");
-			goto err_deinit_port;
+			goto err_remove_irq_domain;
 		}
 	}
 
@@ -1220,9 +1228,11 @@
 	return 0;
 
 err_deinit_port:
-	rockchip_pcie_deinit_phys(rockchip);
+	/* The deferred path takes the PHYs only when user space says so. */
 	if (rockchip->deferred)
 		sysfs_remove_group(&pdev->dev.kobj, &pcie_attr_group);
+	else
+		rockchip_pcie_deinit_phys(rockchip);
 err_remove_irq_domain:
 	irq_domain_remove(rockchip->irq_domain);
 err_vpcie:
